cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its reported results, please cite this repository and record the commit used."
type: software
title: "Counterexample-guided operator coalescing: a controlled study of LLM weight sharing"
authors:
  - family-names: Legotin
    given-names: Artem
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-10-31"
repository-code: "https://github.com/arlegotin/counterexample-guided-operator-coalescing"
url: "https://github.com/arlegotin/counterexample-guided-operator-coalescing"
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Research software for sharing nonlinear feed-forward operators across
  transformer layers with low-rank private corrections. Includes controlled
  local and full-student recovery, activation-weighted initialization,
  composition diagnostics, counterexample probes, complete offline Torch/MLX
  bundles, and source-bound cost and checkpoint records. A rank-8, one-pair,
  one-seed 1024-update diagnostic repairs about 62 percent of initial teacher
  disagreement on exposed development data. The original local pipeline's
  terminal accounting failure remains recorded alongside its independently
  admitted saved state. Twelve matched native artifacts compare an earlier 256-update shared
  checkpoint with dense quantization baselines. No useful
  advantage over strong dense quantization, added counterexample selection
  value, protected capability result or production speedup is established.
  Public numeric receipts can be verified without model weights, corpus access
  or the author's filesystem; optional component bootstrap replay uses NumPy.
keywords:
  - language model compression
  - weight sharing
  - counterexamples
  - low-rank adaptation
  - reproducible research
  - knowledge distillation
  - quantization
